    connections:
      "Ten ideas, one recurring test: did this decision actually run through the myndighet's own independent judgment, or did ministerstyre, formally forbidden but not always easy to detect, quietly shape it instead. Ministerstyre's constitutional prohibition is the foundational structural choice every other concept in this lecture builds on, and meritprincipen's open, decentralized recruitment model shows how Sweden achieves patronage protection through a genuinely different mechanism than the examination-gated systems this course's other entries describe. Offentlighetsprincipen, the world's oldest freedom-of-information guarantee, and the LOU's procurement regime with Konkurrensverket's added systemic oversight are Sweden's own radically transparency-first answers to the exposure points every system in this category has to manage. Mål- och resultatstyrning shows Sweden pioneering, rather than cautiously importing, results-based steering decades before comparable reforms elsewhere, with Statskontoret built in as a standing check against exactly the gaming risk that steering invites, and Riksrevisionen's 2003 move under the Riksdag shows audit independence as a deliberate, relatively recent institutional choice rather than an inevitable feature. Meddelarskydd and visselblåsarlagen together give Sweden a uniquely two-layered whistleblower protection, constitutional and EU-harmonized, while svängdörr shows a system choosing transparency over formal restriction as its primary defense against capture risk. DIGG shows the structural cost of that same agency independence in a different domain, a coordinating body with no power to compel the two hundred independent myndigheter it serves to actually adopt a shared digital standard. The JO closes the loop as the oldest ombudsman institution in the world, combining proactive inspection with a genuine prosecution-referral power that gives Swedish administrative redress a sharper final check than most comparable systems. As you follow any real Swedish administrative controversy from here forward, try asking first whether ministerstyre's line was actually crossed, and then whether offentlighetsprincipen's public record already contains the answer to whatever the controversy is actually about.",
